('16a0f4a6-f9f4-5e8d-9480-bb6643794f06', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'single', 'en', 'A bus covers $90\,\text{km}$ in $2$ hours. What is its average speed in $\text{m/s}$?', '{"options":["$45$","$12.5$","$25$","$7.5$"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":1}'::jsonb, '$45\,\text{km/h} = \frac{45 \times 1000}{3600} = 12.5\,\text{m/s}$.', null, 'original', null, null, 2, array['speed']::text[], true),
('fca1f9b8-3bed-595f-8b5e-dc9bdd281dbb', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'single', 'en', 'A car moving at $20\,\text{m/s}$ brakes and stops in $4\,\text{s}$. What is its acceleration?', '{"options":["$5\\,\\text{m/s}^2$","$-5\\,\\text{m/s}^2$","$80\\,\\text{m/s}^2$","$-80\\,\\text{m/s}^2$"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":1}'::jsonb, '$a = \frac{0 - 20}{4} = -5\,\text{m/s}^2$. The minus sign means the velocity is falling (deceleration).', null, 'original', null, null, 2, array['acceleration']::text[], true),
('48037c0c-67d5-55d8-8b6a-6e6f6311f156', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'single', 'en', 'An object starts from rest with acceleration $2\,\text{m/s}^2$. How far does it go in $5\,\text{s}$?', '{"options":["$10\\,\\text{m}$","$20\\,\\text{m}$","$25\\,\\text{m}$","$50\\,\\text{m}$"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":2}'::jsonb, '$s = ut + \frac{1}{2}at^2 = 0 + \frac{1}{2} \times 2 \times 25 = 25\,\text{m}$.', null, 'original', null, null, 2, array['equations']::text[], true),
('fa06b923-304d-59b0-ad0f-378743501d80', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'single', 'en', 'An object at $10\,\text{m/s}$ speeds up to $30\,\text{m/s}$ with acceleration $2\,\text{m/s}^2$. How far does it go meanwhile?', '{"options":["$100\\,\\text{m}$","$200\\,\\text{m}$","$400\\,\\text{m}$","$250\\,\\text{m}$"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":1}'::jsonb, '$s = \frac{v^2 - u^2}{2a} = \frac{900 - 100}{4} = 200\,\text{m}$.', null, 'original', null, null, 3, array['equations']::text[], true),
('ce3f8f94-6069-5589-b61f-258bcef186bb', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'single', 'en', 'A stone is dropped from a roof. What is its velocity after $2\,\text{s}$? ($g = 9.8\,\text{m/s}^2$)', '{"options":["$4.9\\,\\text{m/s}$","$9.8\\,\\text{m/s}$","$19.6\\,\\text{m/s}$","$39.2\\,\\text{m/s}$"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":2}'::jsonb, '$u = 0$, so $v = gt = 9.8 \times 2 = 19.6\,\text{m/s}$.', null, 'original', null, null, 2, array['free-fall']::text[], true),
('69f55020-2c3d-59ce-81be-6c19c137434b', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'single', 'en', 'A dropped object hits the ground after $3\,\text{s}$. From what height did it fall? ($g = 9.8\,\text{m/s}^2$)', '{"options":["$29.4\\,\\text{m}$","$44.1\\,\\text{m}$","$88.2\\,\\text{m}$","$14.7\\,\\text{m}$"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":1}'::jsonb, '$h = \frac{1}{2}gt^2 = \frac{1}{2} \times 9.8 \times 9 = 44.1\,\text{m}$.', null, 'original', null, null, 3, array['free-fall']::text[], true),
('0129068f-607c-597e-b23e-752135d11e2b', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'single', 'en', 'A man walks $3\,\text{m}$ east, then $4\,\text{m}$ north. What is the size of his displacement?', '{"options":["$7\\,\\text{m}$","$1\\,\\text{m}$","$5\\,\\text{m}$","$12\\,\\text{m}$"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":2}'::jsonb, 'The two legs are at right angles, so displacement $= \sqrt{3^2 + 4^2} = 5\,\text{m}$. The distance is $7\,\text{m}$.', null, 'original', null, null, 3, array['distance-displacement']::text[], true),
('d097e110-0d24-5229-ab7b-7ae8155437b4', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'single', 'en', 'What does the area under a velocity-time graph give?', '{"options":["Acceleration","Distance travelled","Velocity","Time"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":1}'::jsonb, 'Area = velocity × time = distance. The slope of the graph gives acceleration.', null, 'original', null, null, 3, array['graphs']::text[], true),
('6180c1ef-7a76-5481-8f92-ef19f49ad211', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'multi_completion', 'en', 'Consider:

i. Speed is a scalar quantity

ii. An object moving at uniform velocity has zero acceleration

iii. Displacement can never be more than distance

Which is correct?', '{"options":["i and ii","i and iii","ii and iii","i, ii and iii"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":3}'::jsonb, 'All three are true. If velocity does not change, acceleration is zero, and the straight line is the shortest path, so displacement ≤ distance.', null, 'original', null, null, 2, array['scalar-vector']::text[], true),
('34e9429c-f62b-5297-bdb5-16f3d136c958', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'multi_completion', 'en', 'In a vacuum, a feather and an iron ball are dropped together from the same height.

i. Both reach the ground together

ii. The iron ball has the larger acceleration

iii. At any moment both have the same velocity

Which is correct?', '{"options":["i and ii","i and iii","ii and iii","i, ii and iii"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":1}'::jsonb, 'With no air resistance both accelerate at $g$, so i and iii are true; ii is false.', null, 'original', null, null, 3, array['free-fall']::text[], true),
('03a97439-a3c4-5cb9-91be-09841224add6', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'multi_completion', 'en', 'For an object with uniform acceleration:

i. $v = u + at$

ii. $s = \frac{u + v}{2} \times t$

iii. $s = vt$

Which is correct?', '{"options":["i and ii","i and iii","ii and iii","i, ii and iii"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":0}'::jsonb, 'Under uniform acceleration the average velocity is $\frac{u + v}{2}$, so ii holds. $s = vt$ only works for uniform velocity.', null, 'original', null, null, 3, array['equations']::text[], true),
('4ea54bb3-1d36-54da-acb3-a47fef3de2a1', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'situation', 'en', 'What is the train''s velocity after $40\,\text{s}$?', '{"options":["$10\\,\\text{m/s}$","$20\\,\\text{m/s}$","$40\\,\\text{m/s}$","$80\\,\\text{m/s}$"],"context":"A train leaves a station from rest and moves with a uniform acceleration of $0.5\\,\\text{m/s}^2$ for $40\\,\\text{s}$. It then moves at a uniform velocity for the next $60\\,\\text{s}$."}'::jsonb, '{"index":1}'::jsonb, '$v = u + at = 0 + 0.5 \times 40 = 20\,\text{m/s}$.', null, 'original', null, null, 3, array['equations']::text[], true),
('d36c36a7-d3d1-5ab4-a410-6453835a36a0', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'mcq', 'situation', 'en', 'How far does the train go in the whole $100\,\text{s}$?', '{"options":["$400\\,\\text{m}$","$1200\\,\\text{m}$","$1600\\,\\text{m}$","$2000\\,\\text{m}$"],"context":"A train leaves a station from rest and moves with a uniform acceleration of $0.5\\,\\text{m/s}^2$ for $40\\,\\text{s}$. It then moves at a uniform velocity for the next $60\\,\\text{s}$."}'::jsonb, '{"index":2}'::jsonb, 'First part: $\frac{1}{2} \times 0.5 \times 40^2 = 400\,\text{m}$. Second part: $20 \times 60 = 1200\,\text{m}$. Total $1600\,\text{m}$.', null, 'original', null, null, 4, array['equations']::text[], true),
('d3c8290e-7b95-5452-b471-0219da272b85', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'cq', 'cq', 'en', 'Rafi is riding a motorbike at $72\,\text{km/h}$. Suddenly he sees a cow on the road $50\,\text{m}$ ahead and brakes at once. The bike slows with a uniform acceleration of $-5\,\text{m/s}^2$.', null, '[{"part":"a","model":"When an object''s velocity falls over time, the rate at which it falls is called deceleration. It is a negative acceleration.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Correct definition as rate of decrease of velocity or negative acceleration"}]},{"part":"b","model":"Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity, $a = \\frac{v - u}{t}$. At uniform velocity neither the size nor the direction of the velocity changes, so $v = u$.\n\nSo $a = \\frac{u - u}{t} = 0$.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"States acceleration is the rate of change of velocity"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Shows $a = 0$ because velocity does not change"}]},{"part":"c","model":"$u = 72\\,\\text{km/h} = \\frac{72 \\times 1000}{3600} = 20\\,\\text{m/s}$, $v = 0$, $a = -5\\,\\text{m/s}^2$\n\n$v = u + at \\Rightarrow 0 = 20 - 5t$\n\n$t = 4\\,\\text{s}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Converts $72\\,\\text{km/h}$ to $20\\,\\text{m/s}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Substitutes correctly into $v = u + at$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Correct answer $4\\,\\text{s}$"}]},{"part":"d","model":"Distance covered before stopping: $v^2 = u^2 + 2as$\n\n$0 = 20^2 + 2(-5)s \\Rightarrow s = \\frac{400}{10} = 40\\,\\text{m}$\n\nThe cow is $50\\,\\text{m}$ away and the bike stops in $40\\,\\text{m}$. So Rafi stops $10\\,\\text{m}$ short of the cow and avoids it.\n\nIn real life, though, a rider takes a moment to react before braking. During that time the bike keeps going at $20\\,\\text{m/s}$. If the reaction time is more than $0.5\\,\\text{s}$, it goes over $10\\,\\text{m}$ further and hits the cow.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Uses $v^2 = u^2 + 2as$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Gets the stopping distance $40\\,\\text{m}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Compares with $50\\,\\text{m}$ and concludes"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Considers reaction time or another real-world limit"}]}]'::jsonb, null, '[{"part":"a","marks":1,"prompt":"What is deceleration?"},{"part":"b","marks":2,"prompt":"Why is the acceleration of an object moving at uniform velocity zero? Explain."},{"part":"c","marks":3,"prompt":"Find how long the motorbike takes to stop after braking."},{"part":"d","marks":4,"prompt":"Will Rafi avoid hitting the cow? Analyse with a calculation."}]'::jsonb, 'original', null, null, 3, array['equations','deceleration']::text[], true),
('21d9e28f-76b4-5a64-a8e3-de078e55f83d', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'cq', 'cq', 'en', 'A ball is dropped from the roof of a building. It reaches the ground after $4\,\text{s}$. ($g = 9.8\,\text{m/s}^2$; ignore air resistance)', null, '[{"part":"a","model":"The rate at which a freely falling object''s velocity increases because of the Earth''s pull is the acceleration due to gravity. It is about $9.8\\,\\text{m/s}^2$.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Correct definition"}]},{"part":"b","model":"The acceleration $g$ of a falling object does not depend on its mass. In air a feather falls slowly because air resistance affects it much more.\n\nIn a vacuum there is no resistance, so both have the same acceleration $g$ and reach the ground at the same time from the same height.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"States $g$ does not depend on mass"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Explains the role of air resistance"}]},{"part":"c","model":"$u = 0$, $t = 4\\,\\text{s}$, $g = 9.8\\,\\text{m/s}^2$\n\n$h = ut + \\frac{1}{2}gt^2 = 0 + \\frac{1}{2} \\times 9.8 \\times 16$\n\n$h = 78.4\\,\\text{m}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Identifies $u = 0$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Uses $h = \\frac{1}{2}gt^2$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Correct answer $78.4\\,\\text{m}$"}]},{"part":"d","model":"In the first $2\\,\\text{s}$: $h_1 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 9.8 \\times 2^2 = 19.6\\,\\text{m}$\n\nIn the last $2\\,\\text{s}$: $78.4 - 19.6 = 58.8\\,\\text{m}$\n\n$19.6\\,\\text{m}$ is a quarter of the total height, not half.\n\nWhy: the ball gets faster every second, so it covers more ground in each later equal interval. Distance is proportional to $t^2$, so half the time gives $(\\frac{1}{2})^2 = \\frac{1}{4}$ of the distance.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"First $2\\,\\text{s}$ distance $19.6\\,\\text{m}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Compares with the total height"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Concludes it is a quarter, not half"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Explains the reason using $h \\propto t^2$"}]}]'::jsonb, null, '[{"part":"a","marks":1,"prompt":"What is the acceleration due to gravity?"},{"part":"b","marks":2,"prompt":"Why do a feather and a stone fall together in a vacuum? Explain."},{"part":"c","marks":3,"prompt":"Find the height of the building."},{"part":"d","marks":4,"prompt":"Does the ball cover half the height in the first $2\\,\\text{s}$ of its fall? Check and give your view."}]'::jsonb, 'original', null, null, 3, array['free-fall']::text[], true),
('779f74f7-f6b2-50d5-acf2-40ad0feb705a', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'cq', 'cq', 'en', 'A car''s motion:

- $0$ to $10\,\text{s}$: velocity rises uniformly from $0$ to $15\,\text{m/s}$
- $10$ to $30\,\text{s}$: velocity stays at $15\,\text{m/s}$
- $30$ to $35\,\text{s}$: velocity falls uniformly to $0$', null, '[{"part":"a","model":"If an object makes equal displacements in equal times in a fixed direction, its velocity is uniform.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Correct definition"}]},{"part":"b","model":"First stage: $a_1 = \\frac{15 - 0}{10} = 1.5\\,\\text{m/s}^2$\n\nLast stage: $a_3 = \\frac{0 - 15}{5} = -3\\,\\text{m/s}^2$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$a_1 = 1.5\\,\\text{m/s}^2$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$a_3 = -3\\,\\text{m/s}^2$ (with sign)"}]},{"part":"c","model":"The area under the velocity-time graph is the distance.\n\nFirst stage (triangle): $\\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 15 = 75\\,\\text{m}$\n\nMiddle stage (rectangle): $20 \\times 15 = 300\\,\\text{m}$\n\nLast stage (triangle): $\\frac{1}{2} \\times 5 \\times 15 = 37.5\\,\\text{m}$\n\nTotal $= 412.5\\,\\text{m}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Splits into three stages and uses area or equations"},{"points":1,"criterion":"At least two stage distances correct"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Total distance $412.5\\,\\text{m}$"}]},{"part":"d","model":"Average velocity $= \\frac{\\text{total distance}}{\\text{total time}} = \\frac{412.5}{35} \\approx 11.8\\,\\text{m/s}$\n\nThe top speed is $15\\,\\text{m/s}$. The car moved slower than that during the first $10\\,\\text{s}$ and the last $5\\,\\text{s}$; over those $15\\,\\text{s}$ its average was only $7.5\\,\\text{m/s}$.\n\nSo the trip''s average is below the top speed. The shorter the speeding-up and slowing-down times, the closer the average gets to the top speed.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Uses the average velocity formula"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Correct value about $11.8\\,\\text{m/s}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Identifies slower stages as the reason"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Draws a sensible general conclusion"}]}]'::jsonb, null, '[{"part":"a","marks":1,"prompt":"What is uniform velocity?"},{"part":"b","marks":2,"prompt":"Find the car''s acceleration in the first and last stages."},{"part":"c","marks":3,"prompt":"Find the distance the car covers in the full $35\\,\\text{s}$."},{"part":"d","marks":4,"prompt":"If the car had covered the whole trip at one steady speed, what would that average velocity be? Analyse why it is less than the top speed."}]'::jsonb, 'original', null, null, 4, array['graphs','equations']::text[], true),
('e0f74a7b-3702-5076-a56f-ce5d4392fc1f', '1f6187ce-0423-5375-872c-f8baa84b57a1', 'mcq', 'single', 'bn', 'ক্ষতিকর উদ্দেশ্যে তৈরি প্রোগ্রামকে সাধারণভাবে কী বলে?', '{"options":["ফার্মওয়্যার","ম্যালওয়্যার","ফ্রিওয়্যার","মিডলওয়্যার"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":1}'::jsonb, 'Malicious + software = malware। ভাইরাস, ওয়ার্ম, ট্রোজান সবই ম্যালওয়্যার।', null, 'original', null, null, 1, array['malware']::text[], true),
