Which is correct?', '{"options":["i and ii","i and iii","ii and iii","i, ii and iii"]}'::jsonb, '{"index":1}'::jsonb, 'Replying makes things worse. Keep evidence, block and report, and tell an adult.', null, 'original', null, null, 3, array['cyberbullying']::text[], true),
('7245442e-a9b7-58fe-9ebe-28d050a6e5ad', '1f6187ce-0423-5375-872c-f8baa84b57a1', 'mcq', 'situation', 'en', 'What kind of scam is Nabila facing?', '{"options":["Hacking","Phishing","Spamming","Piracy"],"context":"Nabila gets a message: \"Your mobile banking account will be closed. Go to this link now and enter your PIN and OTP.\" The bank''s name in the link address is spelled slightly differently."}'::jsonb, '{"index":1}'::jsonb, 'Pretending to be a known organisation and using a fake link to ask for secret details is phishing.', null, 'original', null, null, 2, array['phishing']::text[], true),
('d896a160-87f3-59e9-af74-5603462c5111', '1f6187ce-0423-5375-872c-f8baa84b57a1', 'mcq', 'situation', 'en', 'What is the best thing for Nabila to do?', '{"options":["Quickly open the link and enter her PIN and OTP","Forward the message to friends","Not open the link, and call the bank''s official number to check","Enter only the PIN, not the OTP"],"context":"Nabila gets a message: \"Your mobile banking account will be closed. Go to this link now and enter your PIN and OTP.\" The bank''s name in the link address is spelled slightly differently."}'::jsonb, '{"index":2}'::jsonb, 'Banks never ask for a PIN or OTP by message. Checking through the official number is safe.', null, 'original', null, null, 3, array['phishing']::text[], true),
('c2644daf-e175-5e88-863d-a605ec865151', '1f6187ce-0423-5375-872c-f8baa84b57a1', 'cq', 'cq', 'en', 'Tanvir brought a pen drive from a friend and opened it on his computer without scanning it. A few days later the computer became very slow and some of his project files would not open. His sister Rima regularly keeps her files on Google Drive and keeps her antivirus updated.', null, '[{"part":"a","model":"A computer virus is a harmful program that attaches itself to other files or programs, copies itself to spread, and damages files or the system.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"States it is a harmful program that spreads by attaching to other files"}]},{"part":"b","model":"A virus needs to attach to another file and becomes active when the user runs that file.\n\nA worm needs no host file; it spreads by itself, sending copies of itself across a network from one computer to another.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Virus depends on a host file"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Worm spreads by itself over a network"}]},{"part":"c","model":"Cause: the friend''s pen drive probably carried a virus. Opening it without scanning let the virus in; it used up the processor and memory (so the computer slowed) and damaged files.\n\nFix: scan the whole computer with updated antivirus software to remove the virus, restore damaged files from a backup if one exists, and scan pen drives before opening them in future.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Identifies virus infection from the pen drive as the cause"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Links it to the slowness and damaged files"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Gives at least two correct fixes"}]},{"part":"d","model":"Rima''s files are safer.\n\nFirst, Rima keeps her antivirus updated, so even new viruses are more likely to be caught. Tanvir opened a pen drive without scanning it.\n\nSecond, Rima has copies of her files on Google Drive (in the cloud). Even if her computer breaks or gets infected, she can get her files back. Tanvir has no backup, so his damaged files may be lost.\n\nStill, the cloud account must be protected with a strong password and two-step verification, or it carries its own risk.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Clearly concludes Rima''s files are safer"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Role of updated antivirus"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Role of the cloud backup"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Considers a limit or extra precaution (password/2FA)"}]}]'::jsonb, null, '[{"part":"a","marks":1,"prompt":"What is a computer virus?"},{"part":"b","marks":2,"prompt":"Explain the difference between a virus and a worm."},{"part":"c","marks":3,"prompt":"Explain the cause of the problem with Tanvir''s computer and how to fix it."},{"part":"d","marks":4,"prompt":"Whose files are safer, Tanvir''s or Rima''s? Evaluate with reasons."}]'::jsonb, 'original', null, null, 3, array['malware','backup']::text[], true),
('98f6b79d-a198-5026-9d50-ed7a34cc7317', '1f6187ce-0423-5375-872c-f8baa84b57a1', 'cq', 'cq', 'en', 'For online classes and games, Sadia uses a laptop about 6 hours a day. She lies in bed with the laptop on her stomach, and at night she turns off the room light and keeps the screen at full brightness. Lately her eyes burn and her neck hurts.', null, '[{"part":"a","model":"Ergonomics is the science of designing and arranging equipment and the workplace to fit the human body.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Correct definition"}]},{"part":"b","model":"After every 20 minutes of screen use, look at something 20 feet (about 6 metres) away for 20 seconds.\n\nLooking at a close screen nonstop keeps the eye muscles tight; looking far away relaxes them and reduces eye strain.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"States the rule correctly"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Explains why it relaxes the eyes"}]},{"part":"c","model":"Neck pain: lying down with the laptop on her stomach puts the screen far below eye level, so she keeps her neck bent forward for a long time. This strains the neck muscles.\n\nBurning eyes: a full-brightness screen in a dark room strains the eyes. On top of that, 6 hours a day without breaks means she blinks less and her eyes dry out.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Links neck pain to poor posture and screen position"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Links eye pain to a bright screen in the dark"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Mentions the effect of long use without breaks"}]},{"part":"d","model":"1. Work at a table and chair: back straight, feet on the floor. Raise the laptop on books or a stand so the top of the screen is at eye level, with a separate keyboard if needed. Then she will not bend her neck.\n\n2. Keep the room light on and set screen brightness close to the room''s light; use night mode at night. This reduces eye strain.\n\n3. Follow the 20-20-20 rule and get up to walk every hour.\n\n4. Limit game time to cut total screen time.\n\nThe plan works because it tackles the root cause of each problem (posture, lighting, nonstop use) directly, and needs no expensive equipment.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Proposes fixing posture and screen height"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Proposes fixing lighting and brightness"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Proposes breaks or less screen time"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Justifies each step by linking it to a cause"}]}]'::jsonb, null, '[{"part":"a","marks":1,"prompt":"What is ergonomics?"},{"part":"b","marks":2,"prompt":"Explain the 20-20-20 rule."},{"part":"c","marks":3,"prompt":"Using the passage, explain why Sadia''s eyes burn and her neck hurts."},{"part":"d","marks":4,"prompt":"Propose a workable plan to fix Sadia''s health problems and analyse why it would work."}]'::jsonb, 'original', null, null, 3, array['ergonomics','eye-care']::text[], true)
on conflict (id) do update set chapter_id = excluded.chapter_id, kind = excluded.kind, subtype = excluded.subtype, medium = excluded.medium, stem = excluded.stem, options_json = excluded.options_json, answer_json = excluded.answer_json, explanation = excluded.explanation, marks_json = excluded.marks_json, source = excluded.source, board = excluded.board, year = excluded.year, difficulty = excluded.difficulty, tags = excluded.tags, published = excluded.published;

insert into public.method_sheets (id, subject_code, chapter_id, question_type, medium, body_md) values
('4c523e65-e98c-522c-aed0-0c2108ca5d07', '109', '2fb8b926-5747-545d-9af6-82cb4940584c', 'x_plus_reciprocal', 'bn', '# $x + \frac{1}{x}$ ধরনের প্রশ্ন

## কীভাবে চিনবে
- প্রশ্নে $x + \frac{1}{x}$ বা $x - \frac{1}{x}$ এর মান দেওয়া থাকে।
- চাওয়া হয় $x^2 + \frac{1}{x^2}$, $x^3 + \frac{1}{x^3}$, $x^4 + \frac{1}{x^4}$ ইত্যাদি।

## ধাপগুলো
1. মনে রাখো $x \cdot \frac{1}{x} = 1$। তাই সূত্রে $ab$ এর জায়গায় সবসময় $1$।
2. বর্গ: $x^2 + \frac{1}{x^2} = (x + \frac{1}{x})^2 - 2$
3. বিয়োগের বর্গ: $(x - \frac{1}{x})^2 = (x + \frac{1}{x})^2 - 4$
4. ঘন: $x^3 + \frac{1}{x^3} = (x + \frac{1}{x})^3 - 3(x + \frac{1}{x})$
5. চতুর্থ ঘাত: $x^4 + \frac{1}{x^4} = (x^2 + \frac{1}{x^2})^2 - 2$
6. প্রতিটি ধাপে আগের ধাপের উত্তর কাজে লাগাও। সৃজনশীলে (ঘ) অংশ প্রায়ই (ক), (খ), (গ) এর উত্তর দিয়ে তৈরি।

## সাধারণ ভুল
- $-2$ এর বদলে $-2x$ লেখা। $2 \cdot x \cdot \frac{1}{x}$ এ $x$ কেটে যায়।
- ঘনের সূত্রে শেষে $-3(x + \frac{1}{x})$ এর বদলে শুধু $-3$ লেখা।

## পাঠের লিংক
বর্গের সূত্র না মনে থাকলে "বর্গের দুটি সূত্র" পাঠটি আবার দেখো।'),
('a798fa55-ae89-526c-aaa1-ef2d7474e6ec', '109', '2fb8b926-5747-545d-9af6-82cb4940584c', 'x_plus_reciprocal', 'en', '# Questions on $x + \frac{1}{x}$

## Spot it
- The question gives the value of $x + \frac{1}{x}$ or $x - \frac{1}{x}$.
- It asks for $x^2 + \frac{1}{x^2}$, $x^3 + \frac{1}{x^3}$, $x^4 + \frac{1}{x^4}$ and so on.

## Steps
1. Remember $x \cdot \frac{1}{x} = 1$, so $ab$ in every formula is $1$.
2. Square: $x^2 + \frac{1}{x^2} = (x + \frac{1}{x})^2 - 2$
3. Square of difference: $(x - \frac{1}{x})^2 = (x + \frac{1}{x})^2 - 4$
4. Cube: $x^3 + \frac{1}{x^3} = (x + \frac{1}{x})^3 - 3(x + \frac{1}{x})$
5. Fourth power: $x^4 + \frac{1}{x^4} = (x^2 + \frac{1}{x^2})^2 - 2$
6. Reuse each answer in the next step. In creative questions, part (d) is often built from (a), (b) and (c).

## Common trap
- Writing $-2x$ instead of $-2$. In $2 \cdot x \cdot \frac{1}{x}$ the $x$ cancels.
- In the cube formula, writing only $-3$ instead of $-3(x + \frac{1}{x})$.

## Lesson link
If the square formulas feel shaky, replay the lesson "Two square formulas".'),
('ffed46d9-d162-5d4e-ac6d-0871cc0f8f7a', '136', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'equations_of_motion', 'bn', '# গতির সমীকরণের অঙ্ক

## কীভাবে চিনবে
- প্রশ্নে আদিবেগ, শেষবেগ, ত্বরণ, সময় বা দূরত্বের মধ্যে তিনটি দেওয়া থাকে, চতুর্থটি চাওয়া হয়।
- "স্থির অবস্থা থেকে", "থেমে গেল", "ছেড়ে দেওয়া হলো" এমন শব্দ থাকে।

## ধাপগুলো
1. জানা রাশিগুলো লেখো: $u$, $v$, $a$, $t$, $s$।
2. লুকানো মান খোঁজো: "স্থির অবস্থা থেকে" মানে $u = 0$, "থেমে গেল" মানে $v = 0$, "ছেড়ে দেওয়া" মানে $u = 0$ ও $a = g$।
3. এককগুলো SI তে আনো। $\text{km/h}$ কে $\text{m/s}$ করতে $\times \frac{5}{18}$।
4. যে রাশি জানা নেই এবং চাওয়াও হয়নি, সেটা যে সমীকরণে নেই সেটা বেছে নাও:
   - $s$ নেই: $v = u + at$
   - $v$ নেই: $s = ut + \frac{1}{2}at^2$
   - $t$ নেই: $v^2 = u^2 + 2as$
5. মান বসাও, একক লিখে উত্তর দাও।
6. সময় থাকলে অন্য একটি সমীকরণ দিয়ে যাচাই করো।

## সাধারণ ভুল
- $\text{km/h}$ থেকে $\text{m/s}$ এ না নিয়েই হিসাব করা।
- বেগ কমলে ত্বরণের ঋণাত্মক চিহ্ন বাদ দেওয়া।
- দুই ধাপের গতিতে (প্রথমে ত্বরণ, পরে সুষম বেগ) পুরো সময়ে একটাই সমীকরণ লাগানো। প্রতিটি ধাপ আলাদা করে হিসাব করো।

## পাঠের লিংক
সমীকরণগুলো কোথা থেকে এল মনে না থাকলে "গতি" পাঠটি আবার দেখো।'),
('a4324c80-f236-5df9-89f4-20a818fbeef6', '136', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'equations_of_motion', 'en', '# Equations of motion problems

## Spot it
- Three of initial velocity, final velocity, acceleration, time and distance are given; a fourth is asked for.
- Words like "from rest", "comes to a stop" or "is dropped" appear.

## Steps
1. List what you know: $u$, $v$, $a$, $t$, $s$.
2. Find the hidden values: "from rest" means $u = 0$, "stops" means $v = 0$, "dropped" means $u = 0$ and $a = g$.
3. Put everything in SI units. To turn $\text{km/h}$ into $\text{m/s}$, multiply by $\frac{5}{18}$.
4. Pick the equation without the quantity you neither know nor need:
   - no $s$: $v = u + at$
   - no $v$: $s = ut + \frac{1}{2}at^2$
   - no $t$: $v^2 = u^2 + 2as$
5. Substitute and give the answer with its unit.
6. If there is time, check with another equation.

## Common trap
- Working in $\text{km/h}$ without converting to $\text{m/s}$.
- Dropping the minus sign on acceleration when the object slows down.
- Using one equation across a two-stage trip (speeding up, then steady). Work each stage separately.

## Lesson link
If you are not sure where the equations come from, replay the lesson "Motion".'),
('0e707e31-53dd-56ad-9d56-90ee6419a7d1', '154', '1f6187ce-0423-5375-872c-f8baa84b57a1', 'ict_situation_cq', 'bn', '# ঘটনাভিত্তিক সৃজনশীল (কম্পিউটার নিরাপত্তা)

## কীভাবে চিনবে
- উদ্দীপকে কোনো চরিত্রের সমস্যা থাকে: কম্পিউটার ধীর, ফাইল নষ্ট, চোখ বা ঘাড়ে ব্যথা, সন্দেহজনক মেসেজ।
- প্রায়ই দুই চরিত্রের তুলনা থাকে: একজন সাবধান, অন্যজন অসাবধান।

## ধাপগুলো
1. (ক) জ্ঞানমূলক: এক বাক্যে সংজ্ঞা। মূল শব্দ বাদ দিয়ো না (যেমন "ক্ষতিকর প্রোগ্রাম", "অন্য ফাইলের সাথে জুড়ে")।
2. (খ) অনুধাবন: দুই বাক্যে ধারণা, তারপর কেন বা কীভাবে।
3. (গ) প্রয়োগ: উদ্দীপক থেকে কারণটি চিহ্নিত করো, পাঠের ধারণার নাম বলো, তারপর ফলাফল মেলাও। "উদ্দীপকে দেখা যায়..." দিয়ে শুরু করো।
4. (ঘ) উচ্চতর দক্ষতা: আগে স্পষ্ট সিদ্ধান্ত (কে বেশি নিরাপদ / কী করা উচিত), তারপর ২-৩টি যুক্তি, শেষে একটি সীমাবদ্ধতা বা বাড়তি সতর্কতা।

## সাধারণ ভুল
- উদ্দীপকের তথ্য ব্যবহার না করে শুধু বই থেকে মুখস্থ লেখা।
- (ঘ) তে সিদ্ধান্ত না দিয়ে শুধু বর্ণনা করা।
- ভাইরাস, ওয়ার্ম ও ট্রোজানের পার্থক্য গুলিয়ে ফেলা।

## পাঠের লিংক
"কম্পিউটার ব্যবহারে নিরাপদ থাকা" পাঠে প্রতিটি ধারণা আছে।'),
('5a7443fd-9676-5bbe-b80b-ebc3d58524e6', '154', '1f6187ce-0423-5375-872c-f8baa84b57a1', 'ict_situation_cq', 'en', '# Situation-based creative questions (computer safety)

## Spot it
- The passage shows someone with a problem: a slow computer, damaged files, sore eyes or neck, a suspicious message.
- Often two people are compared: one careful, one careless.

## Steps
1. (a) Knowledge: a one-sentence definition. Keep the key words (for example "harmful program", "attaches to other files").
2. (b) Comprehension: two sentences on the idea, then why or how.
3. (c) Application: point to the cause in the passage, name the idea from the lesson, then link it to the result. Start with "The passage shows...".
4. (d) Higher-order: a clear conclusion first (who is safer / what should be done), then 2-3 reasons, and finally one limit or extra precaution.

## Common trap
- Writing memorised text without using details from the passage.
- In (d), describing without giving a conclusion.
- Mixing up viruses, worms and Trojans.

## Lesson link
Every idea is in the lesson "Staying safe while using a computer".')
on conflict (id) do update set subject_code = excluded.subject_code, chapter_id = excluded.chapter_id, question_type = excluded.question_type, medium = excluded.medium, body_md = excluded.body_md;

insert into public.drill_templates (id, chapter_id, title, vars_json, constraints_json, solution_js, version) values
('dfcd04b3-5f38-5e8a-b563-a0b43f57d7f0', '2fb8b926-5747-545d-9af6-82cb4940584c', 'Sum of squares from sum and product', '{"a":{"min":1,"max":9},"b":{"min":1,"max":9}}'::jsonb, '["a != b"]'::jsonb, '{"title":{"bn":"যোগফল ও গুণফল থেকে বর্গের যোগফল","en":"Sum of squares from sum and product"},"derived":{"s":"a + b","p":"a * b"},"question":{"bn":"$a + b = {{s}}$ এবং $ab = {{p}}$ হলে, $a^2 + b^2$ এর মান কত?","en":"If $a + b = {{s}}$ and $ab = {{p}}$, what is $a^2 + b^2$?"},"answers":[{"label":{"bn":"$a^2 + b^2$","en":"$a^2 + b^2$"},"expr":"s^2 - 2*p"}],"steps":[{"bn":"সূত্রটি মনে করি: $(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$, তাই $a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab$।","en":"Recall $(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$, so $a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab$."},{"bn":"মান বসাই: $({{s}})^2 - 2 \\times {{p}}$","en":"Substitute: $({{s}})^2 - 2 \\times {{p}}$"},{"bn":"$= {{s^2}} - {{2*p}} = {{s^2 - 2*p}}$","en":"$= {{s^2}} - {{2*p}} = {{s^2 - 2*p}}$"}]}', 1),
('35ed4ebb-b949-51d4-89a8-1464af9980fc', '2fb8b926-5747-545d-9af6-82cb4940584c', 'Expanding the square of a binomial', '{"p":{"min":1,"max":5},"q":{"min":-9,"max":9,"not":[0]}}'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '{"title":{"bn":"দ্বিপদী রাশির বর্গ বিস্তার","en":"Expanding the square of a binomial"},"derived":{"A":"p^2","B":"2*p*q","C":"q^2"},"question":{"bn":"$({{coef:p}}x{{+q}})^2$ কে $Ax^2 + Bx + C$ আকারে লেখো। $A$, $B$ ও $C$ এর মান কত?","en":"Write $({{coef:p}}x{{+q}})^2$ in the form $Ax^2 + Bx + C$. What are $A$, $B$ and $C$?"},"answers":[{"label":{"bn":"$A$","en":"$A$"},"expr":"A"},{"label":{"bn":"$B$","en":"$B$"},"expr":"B"},{"label":{"bn":"$C$","en":"$C$"},"expr":"C"}],"steps":[{"bn":"প্রথম পদ $a = {{coef:p}}x$, দ্বিতীয় পদ $b = {{q}}$। সূত্র: $(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$।","en":"First term $a = {{coef:p}}x$, second term $b = {{q}}$. Formula: $(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$."},{"bn":"$a^2 = ({{coef:p}}x)^2 = {{coef:A}}x^2$, তাই $A = {{A}}$।","en":"$a^2 = ({{coef:p}}x)^2 = {{coef:A}}x^2$, so $A = {{A}}$."},{"bn":"$2ab = 2 \\times {{p}} \\times ({{q}}) \\times x = {{B}}x$, তাই $B = {{B}}$। চিহ্ন খেয়াল করো।","en":"$2ab = 2 \\times {{p}} \\times ({{q}}) \\times x = {{B}}x$, so $B = {{B}}$. Watch the sign."},{"bn":"$b^2 = ({{q}})^2 = {{C}}$, তাই $C = {{C}}$। বর্গ কখনো ঋণাত্মক নয়।","en":"$b^2 = ({{q}})^2 = {{C}}$, so $C = {{C}}$. A square is never negative."}]}', 1),
('57b86a1b-f71c-50f9-9631-8e86818831a1', '111e790d-4f54-5781-82bc-2c877c0315b2', 'Final velocity and distance under uniform acceleration', '{"u":{"min":0,"max":20},"a":{"min":1,"max":5},"t":{"min":2,"max":10}}'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '{"title":{"bn":"সমত্বরণে শেষ বেগ ও দূরত্ব","en":"Final velocity and distance under uniform acceleration"},"derived":{"v":"u + a*t","s":"u*t + a*t^2/2"},"question":{"bn":"একটি বাস ${{u}}\\,\\text{m/s}$ বেগে চলছিল। চালক এক্সেলারেটর চাপায় বাসটি ${{a}}\\,\\text{m/s}^2$ সমত্বরণে আরও ${{t}}\\,\\text{s}$ চলল। (ক) শেষ বেগ কত? (খ) এই সময়ে কত দূরত্ব গেল?","en":"A bus is moving at ${{u}}\\,\\text{m/s}$. The driver accelerates uniformly at ${{a}}\\,\\text{m/s}^2$ for ${{t}}\\,\\text{s}$. (a) What is the final velocity? (b) How far does it go in this time?"},"answers":[{"label":{"bn":"শেষ বেগ $v$","en":"Final velocity $v$"},"expr":"v","unit":{"bn":"m/s","en":"m/s"}},{"label":{"bn":"দূরত্ব $s$","en":"Distance $s$"},"expr":"s","unit":{"bn":"m","en":"m"},"tolerance":0.01}],"steps":[{"bn":"যা জানা আছে: আদি বেগ $u = {{u}}$ m/s, ত্বরণ $a = {{a}}$ m/s², সময় $t = {{t}}$ s।","en":"Known: initial velocity $u = {{u}}$ m/s, acceleration $a = {{a}}$ m/s², time $t = {{t}}$ s."},{"bn":"শেষ বেগ: $v = u + at = {{u}} + {{a}} \\times {{t}} = {{v}}$ m/s","en":"Final velocity: $v = u + at = {{u}} + {{a}} \\times {{t}} = {{v}}$ m/s"},{"bn":"দূরত্ব: $s = ut + \\frac{1}{2}at^2 = {{u}} \\times {{t}} + \\frac{1}{2} \\times {{a}} \\times {{t}}^2 = {{u*t}} + {{a*t^2/2}} = {{s}}$ m","en":"Distance: $s = ut + \\frac{1}{2}at^2 = {{u}} \\times {{t}} + \\frac{1}{2} \\times {{a}} \\times {{t}}^2 = {{u*t}} + {{a*t^2/2}} = {{s}}$ m"},{"bn":"যাচাই: গড় বেগ $\\frac{u + v}{2} \\times t$ দিয়েও একই দূরত্ব পাওয়া যায়।","en":"Check: average velocity $\\frac{u + v}{2} \\times t$ gives the same distance."}]}', 1)
on conflict (id) do update set chapter_id = excluded.chapter_id, title = excluded.title, vars_json = excluded.vars_json, constraints_json = excluded.constraints_json, solution_js = excluded.solution_js, version = excluded.version;

insert into public.mocks (id, subject_code, title, medium, exam_year, duration_mcq_min, duration_cq_min, published, paper_json) values
('e147c613-dd4d-5256-8c7f-7d0bd64f57e6', '109', 'গণিত মডেল টেস্ট ১', 'bn', 2027, 30, 150, true, '{"marks":{"mcq":30,"cq":70},"cq_rules":{"answer":7,"min_per_section":2},"mcq":[{"id":"533e0929-2684-5dfd-936e-58d8edc27c99","subtype":"single","stem":"$\\sqrt{2}$ কোন ধরনের সংখ্যা?","options":["পূর্ণ","অমূলদ","মূলদ","স্বাভাবিক"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$\\sqrt{2}$ কে দুটি পূর্ণসংখ্যার অনুপাতে লেখা যায় না, তাই এটি অমূলদ।"},{"id":"61ab3508-6cf2-5d40-8872-1580dc6016e1","subtype":"single","stem":"$0.\\dot{3}$ কে ভগ্নাংশে প্রকাশ করলে কত হয়?","options":["$\\frac{1}{3}$","$\\frac{3}{10}$","$\\frac{3}{100}$","$\\frac{1}{30}$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"$x = 0.333\\ldots$ হলে $10x - x = 3$, তাই $x = \\frac{1}{3}$।"},{"id":"4b61cdfe-38c6-5096-91f5-5c8dcca7212a","subtype":"single","stem":"$A = \\{1, 2, 3\\}$ হলে $P(A)$ এর উপাদান সংখ্যা কত?","options":["$3$","$6$","$9$","$8$"],"answer":3,"explanation":"$n$ উপাদানের সেটের উপসেট $2^n$টি: $2^3 = 8$।"},{"id":"8b23e5fa-7eaa-52b3-904e-7099198a3503","subtype":"single","stem":"$f(x) = x^2 - 2x$ হলে $f(3)$ এর মান কত?","options":["$-3$","$9$","$3$","$15$"],"answer":2,"explanation":"$f(3) = 9 - 6 = 3$।"},{"id":"696f41c3-653d-592e-b957-e6ba4f83f608","subtype":"single","stem":"$a + b = 5$ এবং $ab = 6$ হলে $a^2 + b^2$ এর মান কত?","options":["$19$","$13$","$25$","$37$"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab = 25 - 12 = 13$।"},{"id":"abd73b26-da4f-5c37-9d0a-c6ac8a81139e","subtype":"single","stem":"$x^2 - 5x + 6$ এর উৎপাদক কোনটি?","options":["$(x - 2)(x - 3)$","$(x + 2)(x + 3)$","$(x - 1)(x - 6)$","$(x + 1)(x - 6)$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"গুণফল $6$ এবং যোগফল $-5$ এমন দুটি সংখ্যা $-2$ ও $-3$।"},{"id":"b22f1170-e693-5342-8701-0ad97c01cc93","subtype":"single","stem":"$2^0 + 2^{-1} = ?$","options":["$\\frac{1}{2}$","$1$","$2$","$\\frac{3}{2}$"],"answer":3,"explanation":"$2^0 = 1$ এবং $2^{-1} = \\frac{1}{2}$, যোগফল $\\frac{3}{2}$।"},{"id":"c7b0b55b-c255-5e76-8416-983bd1983c27","subtype":"single","stem":"$\\log_2 32 = ?$","options":["$6$","$16$","$5$","$4$"],"answer":2,"explanation":"$2^5 = 32$, তাই $\\log_2 32 = 5$।"},{"id":"6cbb119f-fbbd-56ff-b9c2-fcdcbd4f3a9f","subtype":"single","stem":"$3x - 7 = 8$ হলে $x$ এর মান কত?","options":["$-5$","$5$","$3$","$\\frac{1}{3}$"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$3x = 15$, তাই $x = 5$।"},{"id":"f81706da-3c5b-5b82-83e3-3d7849a91e85","subtype":"single","stem":"ত্রিভুজের তিন কোণের সমষ্টি কত?","options":["$180^\\circ$","$90^\\circ$","$270^\\circ$","$360^\\circ$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"যেকোনো ত্রিভুজের তিন কোণের সমষ্টি দুই সমকোণ, অর্থাৎ $180^\\circ$।"},{"id":"3969305c-bd78-5599-836c-ffa8bd8d2a05","subtype":"single","stem":"সমবাহু ত্রিভুজের প্রতিটি কোণ কত?","options":["$30^\\circ$","$45^\\circ$","$90^\\circ$","$60^\\circ$"],"answer":3,"explanation":"তিনটি কোণ সমান এবং সমষ্টি $180^\\circ$, তাই প্রতিটি $60^\\circ$।"},{"id":"359e68ca-f850-5427-8d43-418d4aed40c5","subtype":"single","stem":"অর্ধবৃত্তস্থ কোণ কোন ধরনের কোণ?","options":["স্থূলকোণ","সরলকোণ","সমকোণ","সূক্ষ্মকোণ"],"answer":2,"explanation":"ব্যাসের ওপর দাঁড়ানো বৃত্তস্থ কোণ কেন্দ্রস্থ কোণের ($180^\\circ$) অর্ধেক, অর্থাৎ $90^\\circ$।"},{"id":"df83d353-454b-57fd-8391-8badf9b5b37c","subtype":"single","stem":"$\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = ?$","options":["$\\tan\\theta$","$1$","$0$","$2$"],"answer":1,"explanation":"এটি ত্রিকোণমিতির মৌলিক অভেদ।"},{"id":"c9872e88-4032-581f-bf22-bc82c0a4242c","subtype":"single","stem":"$\\tan 45^\\circ$ এর মান কত?","options":["$1$","$0$","$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$","$\\sqrt{3}$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"$45^\\circ$ কোণে লম্ব ও ভূমি সমান, তাই অনুপাত $1$।"},{"id":"f9d32e7d-1707-5722-86ba-802b993d222a","subtype":"single","stem":"$\\cos 60^\\circ$ এর মান কত?","options":["$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","$1$","$0$","$\\frac{1}{2}$"],"answer":3,"explanation":"সমবাহু ত্রিভুজকে অর্ধেক করলে দেখা যায় $\\cos 60^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2}$।"},{"id":"870a1472-90db-5dd6-b852-5bdcbde93076","subtype":"single","stem":"একটি খুঁটির ছায়ার দৈর্ঘ্য খুঁটির উচ্চতার সমান হলে সূর্যের উন্নতি কোণ কত?","options":["$60^\\circ$","$90^\\circ$","$45^\\circ$","$30^\\circ$"],"answer":2,"explanation":"$\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\text{উচ্চতা}}{\\text{ছায়া}} = 1$, তাই $\\theta = 45^\\circ$।"},{"id":"324d1a4d-90bb-56dd-b4ea-93b475fd74c9","subtype":"single","stem":"$a : b = 2 : 3$ এবং $b : c = 4 : 5$ হলে $a : c$ কত?","options":["$8 : 12$","$8 : 15$","$2 : 5$","$6 : 5$"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$\\frac{a}{c} = \\frac{a}{b} \\cdot \\frac{b}{c} = \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{4}{5} = \\frac{8}{15}$।"},{"id":"998893f2-1d11-570f-8dd3-53eefe1badd7","subtype":"single","stem":"$x + y = 7$ এবং $x - y = 1$ হলে $(x, y)$ কত?","options":["$(4, 3)$","$(3, 4)$","$(5, 2)$","$(6, 1)$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"যোগ করলে $2x = 8$, $x = 4$; তাহলে $y = 3$।"},{"id":"cf2b2388-ef86-5c56-b7c4-ba7b4f35d105","subtype":"single","stem":"প্রথম $10$টি বিজোড় স্বাভাবিক সংখ্যার যোগফল কত?","options":["$81$","$121$","$90$","$100$"],"answer":3,"explanation":"প্রথম $n$টি বিজোড় সংখ্যার যোগফল $n^2 = 100$।"},{"id":"ce84cea6-156d-5cb3-80ae-504f16dc22ba","subtype":"single","stem":"$2, 5, 8, \\ldots$ ধারার $10$ম পদ কত?","options":["$32$","$27$","$29$","$30$"],"answer":2,"explanation":"$a + (n - 1)d = 2 + 9 \\times 3 = 29$।"},{"id":"79662ee6-bc66-5f64-b279-2781844f34ee","subtype":"single","stem":"একটি আয়তক্ষেত্রের দৈর্ঘ্য $8$ সেমি ও প্রস্থ $6$ সেমি হলে কর্ণের দৈর্ঘ্য কত?","options":["$48$ সেমি","$10$ সেমি","$14$ সেমি","$12$ সেমি"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$\\sqrt{8^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{100} = 10$।"},{"id":"bc7a7c02-34cc-5ac5-9852-3e33222d848f","subtype":"single","stem":"$r$ ব্যাসার্ধের বৃত্তের ক্ষেত্রফল কত?","options":["$\\pi r^2$","$2\\pi r$","$\\pi d$","$2\\pi r^2$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"$2\\pi r$ হলো পরিধি; ক্ষেত্রফল $\\pi r^2$।"},{"id":"89430283-9bfa-586c-a245-e55225e8897d","subtype":"single","stem":"একটি ঘনকের এক ধার $3$ সেমি হলে আয়তন কত?","options":["$9$ ঘন সেমি","$18$ ঘন সেমি","$54$ ঘন সেমি","$27$ ঘন সেমি"],"answer":3,"explanation":"$3^3 = 27$।"},{"id":"f6ef8d60-8a13-5667-9793-1f8107a70db7","subtype":"single","stem":"$2, 3, 3, 5, 7$ এর প্রচুরক কত?","options":["$5$","$7$","$3$","$2$"],"answer":2,"explanation":"$3$ সবচেয়ে বেশি বার ($2$ বার) আছে।"},{"id":"d906f415-671d-581e-81f5-ce2c2bd741fb","subtype":"single","stem":"$4, 8, 6, 2$ এর গাণিতিক গড় কত?","options":["$20$","$5$","$4$","$6$"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$\\frac{4 + 8 + 6 + 2}{4} = \\frac{20}{4} = 5$।"},{"id":"5e763cdc-df4a-54f3-8dd8-594845110d43","subtype":"multi_completion","stem":"i. সকল স্বাভাবিক সংখ্যা পূর্ণসংখ্যা\n\nii. সকল পূর্ণসংখ্যা মূলদ সংখ্যা\n\niii. $\\pi$ একটি মূলদ সংখ্যা\n\nনিচের কোনটি সঠিক?","options":["i ও ii","i ও iii","ii ও iii","i, ii ও iii"],"answer":0,"explanation":"$n = \\frac{n}{1}$ বলে প্রতিটি পূর্ণসংখ্যা মূলদ। $\\pi$ অমূলদ, তাই iii ভুল।"},{"id":"f8ae791b-925c-5975-8b69-ff1d4046c253","subtype":"multi_completion","stem":"$\\sin\\theta = \\frac{3}{5}$ এবং $\\theta$ সূক্ষ্মকোণ হলে—\n\ni. $\\cos\\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$\n\nii. $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{4}$\n\niii. $\\sec\\theta = \\frac{5}{4}$\n\nনিচের কোনটি সঠিক?","options":["i ও ii","i ও iii","ii ও iii","i, ii ও iii"],"answer":3,"explanation":"লম্ব $3$, অতিভুজ $5$ হলে ভূমি $4$। তাই $\\cos\\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$, $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{4}$, $\\sec\\theta = \\frac{5}{4}$; তিনটিই সঠিক।"},{"id":"c6ee958f-dd1e-512a-8aaa-80e432a74603","subtype":"multi_completion","stem":"$\\triangle ABC$ এ $\\angle A = 90^\\circ$ হলে—\n\ni. $BC$ বৃহত্তম বাহু\n\nii. $\\angle B$ স্থূলকোণ হতে পারে\n\niii. $\\angle B + \\angle C = 90^\\circ$\n\nনিচের কোনটি সঠিক?","options":["i ও ii","i ও iii","ii ও iii","i, ii ও iii"],"answer":1,"explanation":"সমকোণের বিপরীত বাহু বৃহত্তম। বাকি দুই কোণের সমষ্টি $90^\\circ$, তাই কোনোটিই স্থূলকোণ হতে পারে না।"},{"id":"df76db71-4d5f-5a4f-85a2-43c29089a1f9","subtype":"situation","context":"একটি সমকোণী ত্রিভুজের সমকোণ সংলগ্ন বাহু দুটি $6$ সেমি ও $8$ সেমি।","stem":"ত্রিভুজটির অতিভুজের দৈর্ঘ্য কত?","options":["$14$ সেমি","$10$ সেমি","$12$ সেমি","$7$ সেমি"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$\\sqrt{6^2 + 8^2} = \\sqrt{100} = 10$।"},{"id":"22d63ebf-9293-534a-9fae-152c06ab6026","subtype":"situation","context":"একটি সমকোণী ত্রিভুজের সমকোণ সংলগ্ন বাহু দুটি $6$ সেমি ও $8$ সেমি।","stem":"ত্রিভুজটির ক্ষেত্রফল কত?","options":["$48$ বর্গ সেমি","$14$ বর্গ সেমি","$28$ বর্গ সেমি","$24$ বর্গ সেমি"],"answer":3,"explanation":"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 8 = 24$।"}],"sections":[{"key":"ka","title":"ক বিভাগ: বীজগণিত","cqs":[{"id":"43d5c5a9-5e2d-5995-ad83-4a348e1ec54f","stem":"$x = \\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}$","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"$x^2$ এর মান নির্ণয় করো।","model":"$x^2 = 3 + 2\\sqrt{6} + 2 = 5 + 2\\sqrt{6}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$(a + b)^2$ সূত্র প্রয়োগ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সঠিক মান $5 + 2\\sqrt{6}$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"দেখাও যে, $x + \\frac{1}{x} = 2\\sqrt{3}$ এবং $x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}$ এর মান নির্ণয় করো।","model":"$\\frac{1}{x} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}}{(\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2})} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}}{3 - 2} = \\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}$\n\nতাই $x + \\frac{1}{x} = 2\\sqrt{3}$ (দেখানো হলো)।\n\n$x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = (x + \\frac{1}{x})^2 - 2 = 12 - 2 = 10$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"হরকে মূলদ করে $\\frac{1}{x}$ বের করেছে"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$x + \\frac{1}{x} = 2\\sqrt{3}$ দেখিয়েছে"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সঠিক সূত্র ব্যবহার"},{"points":1,"criterion":"উত্তর $10$"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"$x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3}$ এর মান নির্ণয় করো।","model":"$x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3} = (x + \\frac{1}{x})^3 - 3(x + \\frac{1}{x})$\n\n$= (2\\sqrt{3})^3 - 3 \\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} = 24\\sqrt{3} - 6\\sqrt{3} = 18\\sqrt{3}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"ঘনের সূত্র লিখেছে"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$(2\\sqrt{3})^3 = 24\\sqrt{3}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$3 \\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"উত্তর $18\\sqrt{3}$"}]}]},{"id":"63e45999-6078-549e-85cb-7e1d56323bc9","stem":"$U = \\{1, 2, 3, \\ldots, 10\\}$, $A = \\{x \\in U : x$ জোড় সংখ্যা$\\}$, $B = \\{x \\in U : x$ মৌলিক সংখ্যা$\\}$","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"$A$ ও $B$ কে তালিকা পদ্ধতিতে লেখো এবং $A \\cap B$ নির্ণয় করো।","model":"$A = \\{2, 4, 6, 8, 10\\}$, $B = \\{2, 3, 5, 7\\}$, $A \\cap B = \\{2\\}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$A$ ও $B$ সঠিক"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$A \\cap B = \\{2\\}$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"$(A \\cup B)''$ নির্ণয় করো।","model":"$A \\cup B = \\{2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 10\\}$\n\n$(A \\cup B)'' = U - (A \\cup B) = \\{1, 9\\}$","rubric":[{"points":2,"criterion":"$A \\cup B$ সঠিক"},{"points":1,"criterion":"পূরক সেটের সংজ্ঞা প্রয়োগ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"উত্তর $\\{1, 9\\}$"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"দেখাও যে, $(A \\cup B)'' = A'' \\cap B''$।","model":"$A'' = \\{1, 3, 5, 7, 9\\}$, $B'' = \\{1, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10\\}$\n\n$A'' \\cap B'' = \\{1, 9\\}$\n\n(খ) থেকে $(A \\cup B)'' = \\{1, 9\\}$, তাই $(A \\cup B)'' = A'' \\cap B''$ (দেখানো হলো)।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$A''$ সঠিক"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$B''$ সঠিক"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$A'' \\cap B''$ সঠিক"},{"points":1,"criterion":"দুই পক্ষ মিলিয়ে সিদ্ধান্ত"}]}]},{"id":"c9dc73ec-f53f-5728-995f-07d03c53ff34","stem":"$\\log 2 = 0.3010$ এবং $\\log 3 = 0.4771$ (ভিত্তি $10$)।","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"$\\log_3 81$ এর মান নির্ণয় করো।","model":"$81 = 3^4$, $\\log_3 81 = 4$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$81 = 3^4$ লিখেছে"},{"points":1,"criterion":"উত্তর $4$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"সমাধান করো: $2^{x + 1} = 32$","model":"$32 = 2^5$, তাই $2^{x + 1} = 2^5$\n\nভিত্তি সমান বলে $x + 1 = 5$, $x = 4$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$32 = 2^5$"},{"points":2,"criterion":"সূচক সমান করেছে"},{"points":1,"criterion":"উত্তর $x = 4$"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"$\\log 72$ এর মান নির্ণয় করো।","model":"$72 = 2^3 \\times 3^2$\n\n$\\log 72 = 3\\log 2 + 2\\log 3 = 0.9030 + 0.9542 = 1.8572$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$72 = 2^3 \\times 3^2$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"লগের গুণ ও ঘাতের সূত্র প্রয়োগ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"মান বসিয়েছে"},{"points":1,"criterion":"উত্তর $1.8572$"}]}]},{"id":"a63c5b14-cc23-567c-a5fc-43510fd50080","stem":"সমীকরণজোট: $x + 2y = 8$ এবং $3x - y = 3$","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"$(2, 3)$ প্রথম সমীকরণকে সিদ্ধ করে কি না যাচাই করো।","model":"$2 + 2 \\times 3 = 8$, তাই সিদ্ধ করে।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"মান বসিয়েছে"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সঠিক সিদ্ধান্ত"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"প্রতিস্থাপন পদ্ধতিতে সমীকরণজোটের সমাধান করো।","model":"প্রথমটি থেকে $x = 8 - 2y$। দ্বিতীয়টিতে বসিয়ে $3(8 - 2y) - y = 3$\n\n$24 - 7y = 3$, $y = 3$; তাহলে $x = 8 - 6 = 2$\n\nসমাধান $(x, y) = (2, 3)$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$x$ কে $y$ এর মাধ্যমে প্রকাশ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সঠিকভাবে প্রতিস্থাপন"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$y = 3$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$x = 2$"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"$k$ এর কোন মানের জন্য $x + 2y = 8$ এবং $2x + ky = 5$ সমীকরণজোটের কোনো সমাধান থাকবে না?","model":"সমাধান না থাকার শর্ত: $\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{2}{k} \\neq \\frac{8}{5}$\n\n$\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{2}{k}$ থেকে $k = 4$; এবং $\\frac{1}{2} \\neq \\frac{8}{5}$ সত্য।\n\nতাই $k = 4$ (রেখা দুটি সমান্তরাল)।","rubric":[{"points":2,"criterion":"সঠিক শর্ত লিখেছে"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$k = 4$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"ধ্রুবকের অনুপাত যাচাই করেছে"}]}]}]},{"key":"kha","title":"খ বিভাগ: জ্যামিতি","cqs":[{"id":"9f2dbbbf-28f8-5283-a191-d420fb18493b","stem":"$\\triangle ABC$ এ $AB = AC$ এবং $D$, $BC$ এর মধ্যবিন্দু।","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"$\\angle B = 50^\\circ$ হলে $\\angle A$ নির্ণয় করো।","model":"$AB = AC$ বলে $\\angle C = \\angle B = 50^\\circ$। $\\angle A = 180^\\circ - 100^\\circ = 80^\\circ$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\angle C = 50^\\circ$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\angle A = 80^\\circ$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"প্রমাণ করো যে, $\\triangle ABD \\cong \\triangle ACD$।","model":"$\\triangle ABD$ ও $\\triangle ACD$ এ: $AB = AC$ (দেওয়া আছে), $BD = CD$ ($D$ মধ্যবিন্দু), $AD$ সাধারণ বাহু।\n\nতিন বাহু সমান বলে (বাহু-বাহু-বাহু) $\\triangle ABD \\cong \\triangle ACD$।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$AB = AC$ উল্লেখ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$BD = CD$ কারণসহ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$AD$ সাধারণ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"বাহু-বাহু-বাহু উপপাদ্যে সিদ্ধান্ত"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"প্রমাণ করো যে, $AD \\perp BC$।","model":"(খ) থেকে $\\triangle ABD \\cong \\triangle ACD$, তাই $\\angle ADB = \\angle ADC$।\n\nকিন্তু $\\angle ADB + \\angle ADC = 180^\\circ$ (সরলকোণ)।\n\nতাই প্রতিটি $90^\\circ$, অর্থাৎ $AD \\perp BC$।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"সর্বসমতা থেকে কোণ সমান"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সরলকোণ $180^\\circ$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"প্রতিটি $90^\\circ$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সিদ্ধান্ত"}]}]},{"id":"64094a23-9555-501d-ae1e-d8229a09306b","stem":"$O$ কেন্দ্রবিশিষ্ট বৃত্তের ব্যাসার্ধ $5$ সেমি। $AB$ একটি জ্যা এবং $OM \\perp AB$।","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"$OM = 3$ সেমি হলে $AM$ এর দৈর্ঘ্য নির্ণয় করো।","model":"$AM = \\sqrt{OA^2 - OM^2} = \\sqrt{25 - 9} = 4$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"পিথাগোরাস প্রয়োগ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$AM = 4$ সেমি"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"প্রমাণ করো যে, $AM = MB$।","model":"$O, A$ ও $O, B$ যোগ করি। সমকোণী $\\triangle OMA$ ও $\\triangle OMB$ এ অতিভুজ $OA = OB$ (ব্যাসার্ধ), $OM$ সাধারণ।\n\nসমকোণী ত্রিভুজের অতিভুজ-বাহু উপপাদ্যে $\\triangle OMA \\cong \\triangle OMB$, তাই $AM = MB$।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"অঙ্কন: $OA$, $OB$ যোগ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$OA = OB$ ও $OM$ সাধারণ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"অতিভুজ-বাহু সর্বসমতা"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সিদ্ধান্ত"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"কেন্দ্র থেকে $4$ সেমি দূরের জ্যায়ের দৈর্ঘ্য নির্ণয় করো এবং দেখাও যে কেন্দ্রের নিকটতর জ্যা বৃহত্তর।","model":"দূরত্ব $4$ হলে অর্ধজ্যা $\\sqrt{25 - 16} = 3$, জ্যা $= 6$ সেমি।\n\n(ক) থেকে দূরত্ব $3$ হলে জ্যা $AB = 2 \\times 4 = 8$ সেমি।\n\n$3 < 4$ এবং $8 > 6$, তাই কেন্দ্রের নিকটতর জ্যা বৃহত্তর।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"অর্ধজ্যা $3$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"জ্যা $6$ সেমি"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$AB = 8$ সেমি"},{"points":1,"criterion":"তুলনা করে সিদ্ধান্ত"}]}]},{"id":"5aa96344-86f5-5174-b4f6-2fc2b6a6e5fa","stem":"$ABCD$ একটি আয়তক্ষেত্র, যার কর্ণ $AC$ ও $BD$ পরস্পর $O$ বিন্দুতে ছেদ করে।","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"$AB = 12$ সেমি ও $BC = 5$ সেমি হলে $AC$ নির্ণয় করো।","model":"$AC = \\sqrt{12^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{169} = 13$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"পিথাগোরাস প্রয়োগ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$AC = 13$ সেমি"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"প্রমাণ করো যে, $AC = BD$।","model":"$\\triangle ABC$ ও $\\triangle BAD$ এ: $BC = AD$ (আয়তের বিপরীত বাহু), $AB$ সাধারণ, $\\angle ABC = \\angle BAD = 90^\\circ$।\n\nবাহু-কোণ-বাহু উপপাদ্যে $\\triangle ABC \\cong \\triangle BAD$, তাই $AC = BD$।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$BC = AD$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"অন্তর্ভুক্ত কোণ সমকোণ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"বাহু-কোণ-বাহু"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সিদ্ধান্ত"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"প্রমাণ করো যে, কর্ণদ্বয় পরস্পরকে সমদ্বিখণ্ডিত করে।","model":"$\\triangle AOB$ ও $\\triangle COD$ এ: $AB = CD$, $AB \\parallel CD$ বলে $\\angle OAB = \\angle OCD$ এবং $\\angle OBA = \\angle ODC$ (একান্তর কোণ)।\n\nকোণ-বাহু-কোণ উপপাদ্যে $\\triangle AOB \\cong \\triangle COD$, তাই $OA = OC$ এবং $OB = OD$।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"একান্তর কোণ সমান"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$AB = CD$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"কোণ-বাহু-কোণ সর্বসমতা"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$OA = OC$, $OB = OD$"}]}]},{"id":"4f2e08d7-da16-5060-b5bd-7e30ef36544e","stem":"$O$ কেন্দ্রবিশিষ্ট বৃত্তে $BC$ চাপের ওপর বৃত্তস্থ কোণ $\\angle BAC$ এবং কেন্দ্রস্থ কোণ $\\angle BOC$।","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"$\\angle BOC = 100^\\circ$ হলে $\\angle BAC$ কত?","model":"বৃত্তস্থ কোণ কেন্দ্রস্থ কোণের অর্ধেক: $\\angle BAC = 50^\\circ$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"সম্পর্ক উল্লেখ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$50^\\circ$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"প্রমাণ করো যে, $\\angle BOC = 2\\angle BAC$।","model":"$A, O$ যোগ করে $D$ পর্যন্ত বাড়াই। $\\triangle AOB$ এ $OA = OB$, তাই $\\angle OAB = \\angle OBA$।\n\nবহিঃস্থ কোণ $\\angle BOD = \\angle OAB + \\angle OBA = 2\\angle OAB$।\n\nএকইভাবে $\\angle COD = 2\\angle OAC$।\n\nযোগ করে $\\angle BOC = 2(\\angle OAB + \\angle OAC) = 2\\angle BAC$।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"অঙ্কন: $AO$ বর্ধিত"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সমদ্বিবাহু ত্রিভুজের কোণ সমান"},{"points":1,"criterion":"বহিঃস্থ কোণের উপপাদ্য"},{"points":1,"criterion":"যোগ করে সিদ্ধান্ত"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"$ABCD$ বৃত্তে অন্তর্লিখিত চতুর্ভুজ হলে প্রমাণ করো যে, $\\angle A + \\angle C = 180^\\circ$।","model":"$O$ এর সাথে $B$ ও $D$ যোগ করি। (খ) অনুযায়ী $BCD$ চাপের ওপর কেন্দ্রস্থ কোণ $= 2\\angle A$ এবং $BAD$ চাপের ওপর প্রবৃদ্ধ কেন্দ্রস্থ কোণ $= 2\\angle C$।\n\nকেন্দ্রে মোট কোণ $360^\\circ$: $2\\angle A + 2\\angle C = 360^\\circ$\n\nতাই $\\angle A + \\angle C = 180^\\circ$।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"অঙ্কন"},{"points":1,"criterion":"কেন্দ্রস্থ কোণ $2\\angle A$ ও $2\\angle C$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সমষ্টি $360^\\circ$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সিদ্ধান্ত"}]}]}]},{"key":"ga","title":"গ বিভাগ: ত্রিকোণমিতি ও পরিমিতি","cqs":[{"id":"2b6c7d2b-0db1-5a6c-a506-b004d152334f","stem":"$\\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{4}$, যেখানে $\\theta$ সূক্ষ্মকোণ।","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"$\\sin\\theta$ ও $\\cos\\theta$ এর মান নির্ণয় করো।","model":"লম্ব $3$, ভূমি $4$, অতিভুজ $5$। $\\sin\\theta = \\frac{3}{5}$, $\\cos\\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"অতিভুজ $5$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"দুটি মান সঠিক"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"$\\frac{1 - \\tan^2\\theta}{1 + \\tan^2\\theta}$ এবং $\\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta$ এর মান নির্ণয় করে তুলনা করো।","model":"$\\frac{1 - \\frac{9}{16}}{1 + \\frac{9}{16}} = \\frac{7/16}{25/16} = \\frac{7}{25}$\n\n$\\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta = \\frac{16}{25} - \\frac{9}{25} = \\frac{7}{25}$\n\nদুটি মান সমান।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"প্রথম রাশিতে মান বসানো"},{"points":1,"criterion":"প্রথম মান $\\frac{7}{25}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"দ্বিতীয় মান $\\frac{7}{25}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"তুলনা"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"যেকোনো সূক্ষ্মকোণ $\\theta$ এর জন্য প্রমাণ করো: $\\frac{1 - \\tan^2\\theta}{1 + \\tan^2\\theta} = \\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta$","model":"বামপক্ষে লব ও হরকে $\\cos^2\\theta$ দিয়ে গুণ করি:\n\n$\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta} = \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta}{1} = $ ডানপক্ষ (প্রমাণিত)","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ ব্যবহার"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\cos^2\\theta$ দিয়ে গুণ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"সিদ্ধান্ত"}]}]},{"id":"55fd573a-6f82-5c42-ab72-4b7b048dda9d","stem":"একটি গাছের গোড়া থেকে $30$ মিটার দূরে মাটির একটি বিন্দু থেকে গাছের মাথার উন্নতি কোণ $60^\\circ$।","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"তথ্যটি চিত্রে দেখাও এবং গাছের উচ্চতা $h$ এর সাথে সম্পর্কটি লেখো।","model":"সমকোণী ত্রিভুজে ভূমি $30$ মিটার, লম্ব $h$, উন্নতি কোণ $60^\\circ$। $\\tan 60^\\circ = \\frac{h}{30}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"সঠিক চিত্র"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\tan 60^\\circ = \\frac{h}{30}$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"গাছের উচ্চতা নির্ণয় করো।","model":"$h = 30\\tan 60^\\circ = 30\\sqrt{3} \\approx 51.96$ মিটার","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\tan 60^\\circ = \\sqrt{3}$"},{"points":2,"criterion":"$h = 30\\sqrt{3}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"আসন্ন মান $51.96$ মিটার"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"বিন্দুটি থেকে গাছের দিক থেকে সরাসরি আর কত মিটার দূরে গেলে উন্নতি কোণ $30^\\circ$ হবে?","model":"নতুন দূরত্ব $d$ হলে $\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{h}{d}$, $d = h\\sqrt{3} = 30\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = 90$ মিটার।\n\nআরও যেতে হবে $90 - 30 = 60$ মিটার।","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{h}{d}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$d = 90$ মিটার"},{"points":1,"criterion":"পার্থক্য নেওয়া"},{"points":1,"criterion":"উত্তর $60$ মিটার"}]}]},{"id":"fcaa333c-e6a1-50b4-adf2-c58de0346277","stem":"একটি আয়তাকার মাঠের দৈর্ঘ্য $40$ মিটার ও প্রস্থ $30$ মিটার। মাঠের ভেতরে চারদিক ঘিরে $2$ মিটার চওড়া একটি রাস্তা আছে।","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"মাঠের ক্ষেত্রফল ও কর্ণের দৈর্ঘ্য নির্ণয় করো।","model":"ক্ষেত্রফল $40 \\times 30 = 1200$ বর্গমিটার; কর্ণ $\\sqrt{40^2 + 30^2} = 50$ মিটার","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"ক্ষেত্রফল $1200$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"কর্ণ $50$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"রাস্তার ক্ষেত্রফল নির্ণয় করো।","model":"ভেতরের অংশ: $(40 - 4) \\times (30 - 4) = 36 \\times 26 = 936$ বর্গমিটার\n\nরাস্তা: $1200 - 936 = 264$ বর্গমিটার","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"ভেতরের মাপ $36$ ও $26$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"ভেতরের ক্ষেত্রফল $936$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"বিয়োগ"},{"points":1,"criterion":"উত্তর $264$"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"প্রতি বর্গমিটারে $50$ টাকা হিসেবে রাস্তা ইট দিয়ে বাঁধাতে কত খরচ হবে? প্রতিটি ইট $0.05$ বর্গমিটার জায়গা ঢাকলে কয়টি ইট লাগবে?","model":"খরচ $264 \\times 50 = 13200$ টাকা\n\nইট $\\frac{264}{0.05} = 5280$টি","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"খরচের হিসাব"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$13200$ টাকা"},{"points":1,"criterion":"ইটের হিসাব"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$5280$টি"}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb),
('927fb4e9-20c2-5670-9a9c-c5145948765c', '109', 'Mathematics model test 1', 'en', 2027, 30, 150, true, '{"marks":{"mcq":30,"cq":70},"cq_rules":{"answer":7,"min_per_section":2},"mcq":[{"id":"10c430f9-4e23-51b6-bb5f-9364efca150e","subtype":"single","stem":"What kind of number is $\\sqrt{2}$?","options":["Integer","Irrational","Rational","Natural"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$\\sqrt{2}$ cannot be written as a ratio of two integers, so it is irrational."},{"id":"80c99e88-0a56-54fc-bf9c-40a2b320a811","subtype":"single","stem":"Written as a fraction, $0.\\dot{3}$ is","options":["$\\frac{1}{3}$","$\\frac{3}{10}$","$\\frac{3}{100}$","$\\frac{1}{30}$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"If $x = 0.333\\ldots$ then $10x - x = 3$, so $x = \\frac{1}{3}$."},{"id":"2b295fbc-d141-5125-8788-401ce50b5bc4","subtype":"single","stem":"If $A = \\{1, 2, 3\\}$, how many elements does $P(A)$ have?","options":["$3$","$6$","$9$","$8$"],"answer":3,"explanation":"A set with $n$ elements has $2^n$ subsets: $2^3 = 8$."},{"id":"87819194-ed00-5cdd-b159-b6e6798ee2d1","subtype":"single","stem":"If $f(x) = x^2 - 2x$, what is $f(3)$?","options":["$-3$","$9$","$3$","$15$"],"answer":2,"explanation":"$f(3) = 9 - 6 = 3$."},{"id":"8d57fb2b-94b9-599a-a57a-083bdcc35987","subtype":"single","stem":"If $a + b = 5$ and $ab = 6$, what is $a^2 + b^2$?","options":["$19$","$13$","$25$","$37$"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab = 25 - 12 = 13$."},{"id":"6c03ac2d-2ba7-5851-a0b3-7d9719294dc1","subtype":"single","stem":"Which is the factorisation of $x^2 - 5x + 6$?","options":["$(x - 2)(x - 3)$","$(x + 2)(x + 3)$","$(x - 1)(x - 6)$","$(x + 1)(x - 6)$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Two numbers with product $6$ and sum $-5$ are $-2$ and $-3$."},{"id":"bb9239d2-0f33-5a38-8063-942b3465c5e1","subtype":"single","stem":"$2^0 + 2^{-1} = ?$","options":["$\\frac{1}{2}$","$1$","$2$","$\\frac{3}{2}$"],"answer":3,"explanation":"$2^0 = 1$ and $2^{-1} = \\frac{1}{2}$, so the sum is $\\frac{3}{2}$."},{"id":"8c702336-03e0-5aa7-9ae3-53de50cf9567","subtype":"single","stem":"$\\log_2 32 = ?$","options":["$6$","$16$","$5$","$4$"],"answer":2,"explanation":"$2^5 = 32$, so $\\log_2 32 = 5$."},{"id":"cd4cf4a8-fd96-5253-98b2-6ce58d6512df","subtype":"single","stem":"If $3x - 7 = 8$, what is $x$?","options":["$-5$","$5$","$3$","$\\frac{1}{3}$"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$3x = 15$, so $x = 5$."},{"id":"b08fdf7c-4f17-52e4-a264-ed80e8023125","subtype":"single","stem":"What is the sum of the three angles of a triangle?","options":["$180^\\circ$","$90^\\circ$","$270^\\circ$","$360^\\circ$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"The angles of any triangle add up to two right angles, $180^\\circ$."},{"id":"5557ee9b-f6ea-5af9-8e10-3c2ab15d5c0b","subtype":"single","stem":"Each angle of an equilateral triangle is","options":["$30^\\circ$","$45^\\circ$","$90^\\circ$","$60^\\circ$"],"answer":3,"explanation":"All three angles are equal and add to $180^\\circ$, so each is $60^\\circ$."},{"id":"64b30051-2f20-53ac-9ffe-b5bb39aaf66c","subtype":"single","stem":"An angle in a semicircle is","options":["an obtuse angle","a straight angle","a right angle","an acute angle"],"answer":2,"explanation":"It is half the centre angle on the diameter ($180^\\circ$), so $90^\\circ$."},{"id":"4d62522d-50f4-51d9-a906-a844c8e59a08","subtype":"single","stem":"$\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = ?$","options":["$\\tan\\theta$","$1$","$0$","$2$"],"answer":1,"explanation":"This is the basic trigonometric identity."},{"id":"5fbf055f-d207-5092-b545-c963c223c9f3","subtype":"single","stem":"What is $\\tan 45^\\circ$?","options":["$1$","$0$","$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$","$\\sqrt{3}$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"At $45^\\circ$ the opposite and adjacent sides are equal, so the ratio is $1$."},{"id":"748e581e-a629-5272-a5fd-82bc3794fdf3","subtype":"single","stem":"What is $\\cos 60^\\circ$?","options":["$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$","$1$","$0$","$\\frac{1}{2}$"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Halving an equilateral triangle shows $\\cos 60^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2}$."},{"id":"e1a2a5de-ea19-50b9-a341-4aecebf694d9","subtype":"single","stem":"When a pole''s shadow is as long as the pole is tall, the sun''s angle of elevation is","options":["$60^\\circ$","$90^\\circ$","$45^\\circ$","$30^\\circ$"],"answer":2,"explanation":"$\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\text{height}}{\\text{shadow}} = 1$, so $\\theta = 45^\\circ$."},{"id":"112564c3-f9f2-5848-a413-fe3618a50270","subtype":"single","stem":"If $a : b = 2 : 3$ and $b : c = 4 : 5$, then $a : c$ is","options":["$8 : 12$","$8 : 15$","$2 : 5$","$6 : 5$"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$\\frac{a}{c} = \\frac{a}{b} \\cdot \\frac{b}{c} = \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{4}{5} = \\frac{8}{15}$."},{"id":"d4d19446-4ba0-51db-9bcb-85b49e32a273","subtype":"single","stem":"If $x + y = 7$ and $x - y = 1$, then $(x, y)$ is","options":["$(4, 3)$","$(3, 4)$","$(5, 2)$","$(6, 1)$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Adding gives $2x = 8$, $x = 4$; then $y = 3$."},{"id":"2b75c619-b3ad-58e7-b7b0-731d877a8adf","subtype":"single","stem":"What is the sum of the first $10$ odd natural numbers?","options":["$81$","$121$","$90$","$100$"],"answer":3,"explanation":"The sum of the first $n$ odd numbers is $n^2 = 100$."},{"id":"b2a1cd03-5ab9-5cba-84e1-80798cc726c7","subtype":"single","stem":"What is the $10$th term of $2, 5, 8, \\ldots$?","options":["$32$","$27$","$29$","$30$"],"answer":2,"explanation":"$a + (n - 1)d = 2 + 9 \\times 3 = 29$."},{"id":"116a538a-85ba-5ab4-a33a-f9489cb7464d","subtype":"single","stem":"A rectangle is $8$ cm long and $6$ cm wide. How long is its diagonal?","options":["$48$ cm","$10$ cm","$14$ cm","$12$ cm"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$\\sqrt{8^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{100} = 10$."},{"id":"c4ab674d-1713-50b7-8fd1-2a4333c2a220","subtype":"single","stem":"The area of a circle of radius $r$ is","options":["$\\pi r^2$","$2\\pi r$","$\\pi d$","$2\\pi r^2$"],"answer":0,"explanation":"$2\\pi r$ is the circumference; the area is $\\pi r^2$."},{"id":"d14b2901-31a9-51fd-a9e0-558cfe5aa1b9","subtype":"single","stem":"A cube has edge $3$ cm. What is its volume?","options":["$9$ cm³","$18$ cm³","$54$ cm³","$27$ cm³"],"answer":3,"explanation":"$3^3 = 27$."},{"id":"d8eb02ef-dd2b-52b5-b873-964c1f1fd366","subtype":"single","stem":"What is the mode of $2, 3, 3, 5, 7$?","options":["$5$","$7$","$3$","$2$"],"answer":2,"explanation":"$3$ appears most often (twice)."},{"id":"254d683b-7bc8-518e-8af0-bc9ce1863a04","subtype":"single","stem":"What is the mean of $4, 8, 6, 2$?","options":["$20$","$5$","$4$","$6$"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$\\frac{4 + 8 + 6 + 2}{4} = \\frac{20}{4} = 5$."},{"id":"6d161ac4-38ab-5a73-9d7f-aba0fc75a8c2","subtype":"multi_completion","stem":"i. Every natural number is an integer\n\nii. Every integer is a rational number\n\niii. $\\pi$ is a rational number\n\nWhich is correct?","options":["i and ii","i and iii","ii and iii","i, ii and iii"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Every integer is rational because $n = \\frac{n}{1}$. $\\pi$ is irrational, so iii is wrong."},{"id":"234c2009-8b63-54b8-be54-7dbfb972bd43","subtype":"multi_completion","stem":"If $\\sin\\theta = \\frac{3}{5}$ and $\\theta$ is acute:\n\ni. $\\cos\\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$\n\nii. $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{4}$\n\niii. $\\sec\\theta = \\frac{5}{4}$\n\nWhich is correct?","options":["i and ii","i and iii","ii and iii","i, ii and iii"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Opposite $3$, hypotenuse $5$ gives adjacent $4$. So $\\cos\\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$, $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{4}$, $\\sec\\theta = \\frac{5}{4}$: all three are right."},{"id":"967ff517-783a-56d6-86ae-6c9692b78239","subtype":"multi_completion","stem":"In $\\triangle ABC$, $\\angle A = 90^\\circ$:\n\ni. $BC$ is the longest side\n\nii. $\\angle B$ can be obtuse\n\niii. $\\angle B + \\angle C = 90^\\circ$\n\nWhich is correct?","options":["i and ii","i and iii","ii and iii","i, ii and iii"],"answer":1,"explanation":"The side opposite the right angle is longest. The other two angles add to $90^\\circ$, so neither can be obtuse."},{"id":"92cb8fab-daf4-5521-a5d5-8597b1966ce1","subtype":"situation","context":"The two sides next to the right angle of a right triangle are $6$ cm and $8$ cm.","stem":"How long is the hypotenuse?","options":["$14$ cm","$10$ cm","$12$ cm","$7$ cm"],"answer":1,"explanation":"$\\sqrt{6^2 + 8^2} = \\sqrt{100} = 10$."},{"id":"0b229f4b-4124-53f1-a090-189abf2c5ab2","subtype":"situation","context":"The two sides next to the right angle of a right triangle are $6$ cm and $8$ cm.","stem":"What is the area of the triangle?","options":["$48$ cm²","$14$ cm²","$28$ cm²","$24$ cm²"],"answer":3,"explanation":"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 8 = 24$."}],"sections":[{"key":"ka","title":"Section A: Algebra","cqs":[{"id":"0a401198-c671-5e77-b5be-2bcb444d053c","stem":"$x = \\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}$","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"Find $x^2$.","model":"$x^2 = 3 + 2\\sqrt{6} + 2 = 5 + 2\\sqrt{6}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Uses $(a + b)^2$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Correct value $5 + 2\\sqrt{6}$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"Show that $x + \\frac{1}{x} = 2\\sqrt{3}$ and find $x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2}$.","model":"$\\frac{1}{x} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}}{(\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2})} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}}{3 - 2} = \\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}$\n\nSo $x + \\frac{1}{x} = 2\\sqrt{3}$ (shown).\n\n$x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = (x + \\frac{1}{x})^2 - 2 = 12 - 2 = 10$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Rationalises to get $\\frac{1}{x}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Shows $x + \\frac{1}{x} = 2\\sqrt{3}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Uses the right identity"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Answer $10$"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"Find $x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3}$.","model":"$x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3} = (x + \\frac{1}{x})^3 - 3(x + \\frac{1}{x})$\n\n$= (2\\sqrt{3})^3 - 3 \\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} = 24\\sqrt{3} - 6\\sqrt{3} = 18\\sqrt{3}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Writes the cube identity"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$(2\\sqrt{3})^3 = 24\\sqrt{3}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$3 \\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Answer $18\\sqrt{3}$"}]}]},{"id":"17a6e746-553e-5315-af99-df96722edf12","stem":"$U = \\{1, 2, 3, \\ldots, 10\\}$, $A = \\{x \\in U : x$ is even$\\}$, $B = \\{x \\in U : x$ is prime$\\}$","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"List $A$ and $B$ and find $A \\cap B$.","model":"$A = \\{2, 4, 6, 8, 10\\}$, $B = \\{2, 3, 5, 7\\}$, $A \\cap B = \\{2\\}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$A$ and $B$ correct"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$A \\cap B = \\{2\\}$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"Find $(A \\cup B)''$.","model":"$A \\cup B = \\{2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 10\\}$\n\n$(A \\cup B)'' = U - (A \\cup B) = \\{1, 9\\}$","rubric":[{"points":2,"criterion":"$A \\cup B$ correct"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Uses the complement definition"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Answer $\\{1, 9\\}$"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"Show that $(A \\cup B)'' = A'' \\cap B''$.","model":"$A'' = \\{1, 3, 5, 7, 9\\}$, $B'' = \\{1, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10\\}$\n\n$A'' \\cap B'' = \\{1, 9\\}$\n\nFrom (b), $(A \\cup B)'' = \\{1, 9\\}$, so $(A \\cup B)'' = A'' \\cap B''$ (shown).","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$A''$ correct"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$B''$ correct"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$A'' \\cap B''$ correct"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Compares both sides and concludes"}]}]},{"id":"17d60e7b-7617-5655-bc1f-39e24398bc4b","stem":"$\\log 2 = 0.3010$ and $\\log 3 = 0.4771$ (base $10$).","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"Find $\\log_3 81$.","model":"$81 = 3^4$, $\\log_3 81 = 4$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Writes $81 = 3^4$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Answer $4$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"Solve: $2^{x + 1} = 32$","model":"$32 = 2^5$, so $2^{x + 1} = 2^5$\n\nThe bases are equal, so $x + 1 = 5$, $x = 4$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$32 = 2^5$"},{"points":2,"criterion":"Equates the exponents"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Answer $x = 4$"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"Find $\\log 72$.","model":"$72 = 2^3 \\times 3^2$\n\n$\\log 72 = 3\\log 2 + 2\\log 3 = 0.9030 + 0.9542 = 1.8572$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$72 = 2^3 \\times 3^2$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Uses product and power rules"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Substitutes the values"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Answer $1.8572$"}]}]},{"id":"483390f3-80b6-5dbb-aa3e-d02af849748d","stem":"Equations: $x + 2y = 8$ and $3x - y = 3$","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"Check whether $(2, 3)$ satisfies the first equation.","model":"$2 + 2 \\times 3 = 8$, so it does.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Substitutes"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Correct conclusion"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"Solve the pair by substitution.","model":"From the first, $x = 8 - 2y$. Put it in the second: $3(8 - 2y) - y = 3$\n\n$24 - 7y = 3$, $y = 3$; then $x = 8 - 6 = 2$\n\nSolution $(x, y) = (2, 3)$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Expresses $x$ in terms of $y$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Substitutes correctly"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$y = 3$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$x = 2$"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"For what value of $k$ do $x + 2y = 8$ and $2x + ky = 5$ have no solution?","model":"Condition for no solution: $\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{2}{k} \\neq \\frac{8}{5}$\n\n$\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{2}{k}$ gives $k = 4$; and $\\frac{1}{2} \\neq \\frac{8}{5}$ holds.\n\nSo $k = 4$ (the lines are parallel).","rubric":[{"points":2,"criterion":"Writes the correct condition"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$k = 4$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Checks the constant ratio"}]}]}]},{"key":"kha","title":"Section B: Geometry","cqs":[{"id":"95fc7110-6562-5e69-ab1e-259f5e5d0495","stem":"In $\\triangle ABC$, $AB = AC$ and $D$ is the midpoint of $BC$.","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"If $\\angle B = 50^\\circ$, find $\\angle A$.","model":"Since $AB = AC$, $\\angle C = \\angle B = 50^\\circ$. $\\angle A = 180^\\circ - 100^\\circ = 80^\\circ$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\angle C = 50^\\circ$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\angle A = 80^\\circ$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"Prove that $\\triangle ABD \\cong \\triangle ACD$.","model":"In $\\triangle ABD$ and $\\triangle ACD$: $AB = AC$ (given), $BD = CD$ ($D$ is the midpoint), $AD$ is common.\n\nThree sides equal (SSS), so $\\triangle ABD \\cong \\triangle ACD$.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"States $AB = AC$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$BD = CD$ with reason"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$AD$ common"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Concludes by SSS"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"Prove that $AD \\perp BC$.","model":"From (b), $\\triangle ABD \\cong \\triangle ACD$, so $\\angle ADB = \\angle ADC$.\n\nBut $\\angle ADB + \\angle ADC = 180^\\circ$ (straight angle).\n\nSo each is $90^\\circ$, i.e. $AD \\perp BC$.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Equal angles from congruence"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Straight angle $180^\\circ$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Each is $90^\\circ$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Conclusion"}]}]},{"id":"4ee45f71-17df-50a3-b0c7-0b074a3dee43","stem":"A circle with centre $O$ has radius $5$ cm. $AB$ is a chord and $OM \\perp AB$.","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"If $OM = 3$ cm, find $AM$.","model":"$AM = \\sqrt{OA^2 - OM^2} = \\sqrt{25 - 9} = 4$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Uses Pythagoras"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$AM = 4$ cm"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"Prove that $AM = MB$.","model":"Join $OA$ and $OB$. In right triangles $OMA$ and $OMB$, hypotenuses $OA = OB$ (radii) and $OM$ is common.\n\nBy RHS, $\\triangle OMA \\cong \\triangle OMB$, so $AM = MB$.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Construction: join $OA$, $OB$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$OA = OB$ and $OM$ common"},{"points":1,"criterion":"RHS congruence"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Conclusion"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"Find the length of a chord $4$ cm from the centre, and show that the chord nearer the centre is longer.","model":"At distance $4$, half-chord $= \\sqrt{25 - 16} = 3$, so the chord is $6$ cm.\n\nFrom (a), at distance $3$ the chord $AB = 2 \\times 4 = 8$ cm.\n\n$3 < 4$ and $8 > 6$, so the chord nearer the centre is longer.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Half-chord $3$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Chord $6$ cm"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$AB = 8$ cm"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Compares and concludes"}]}]},{"id":"b3efba99-ed8f-50eb-b7de-1e445f150b04","stem":"$ABCD$ is a rectangle whose diagonals $AC$ and $BD$ meet at $O$.","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"If $AB = 12$ cm and $BC = 5$ cm, find $AC$.","model":"$AC = \\sqrt{12^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{169} = 13$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Uses Pythagoras"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$AC = 13$ cm"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"Prove that $AC = BD$.","model":"In $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle BAD$: $BC = AD$ (opposite sides), $AB$ common, $\\angle ABC = \\angle BAD = 90^\\circ$.\n\nBy SAS, $\\triangle ABC \\cong \\triangle BAD$, so $AC = BD$.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$BC = AD$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Included angles are right angles"},{"points":1,"criterion":"SAS"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Conclusion"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"Prove that the diagonals bisect each other.","model":"In $\\triangle AOB$ and $\\triangle COD$: $AB = CD$, and since $AB \\parallel CD$, $\\angle OAB = \\angle OCD$ and $\\angle OBA = \\angle ODC$ (alternate angles).\n\nBy ASA, $\\triangle AOB \\cong \\triangle COD$, so $OA = OC$ and $OB = OD$.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Alternate angles equal"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$AB = CD$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"ASA congruence"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$OA = OC$, $OB = OD$"}]}]},{"id":"e874c737-74bd-5b53-9cba-c8c80da2b92c","stem":"In a circle with centre $O$, arc $BC$ makes the inscribed angle $\\angle BAC$ and the centre angle $\\angle BOC$.","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"If $\\angle BOC = 100^\\circ$, find $\\angle BAC$.","model":"The inscribed angle is half the centre angle: $\\angle BAC = 50^\\circ$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"States the relation"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$50^\\circ$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"Prove that $\\angle BOC = 2\\angle BAC$.","model":"Join $AO$ and extend it to $D$. In $\\triangle AOB$, $OA = OB$, so $\\angle OAB = \\angle OBA$.\n\nExterior angle $\\angle BOD = \\angle OAB + \\angle OBA = 2\\angle OAB$.\n\nSimilarly $\\angle COD = 2\\angle OAC$.\n\nAdding, $\\angle BOC = 2(\\angle OAB + \\angle OAC) = 2\\angle BAC$.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Construction: extend $AO$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Base angles of isosceles triangle"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Exterior angle theorem"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Adds and concludes"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"If $ABCD$ is a cyclic quadrilateral, prove that $\\angle A + \\angle C = 180^\\circ$.","model":"Join $OB$ and $OD$. By (b), the centre angle on arc $BCD$ is $2\\angle A$ and the reflex centre angle on arc $BAD$ is $2\\angle C$.\n\nAngles at the centre total $360^\\circ$: $2\\angle A + 2\\angle C = 360^\\circ$\n\nSo $\\angle A + \\angle C = 180^\\circ$.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Construction"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Centre angles $2\\angle A$ and $2\\angle C$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Sum $360^\\circ$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Conclusion"}]}]}]},{"key":"ga","title":"Section C: Trigonometry and mensuration","cqs":[{"id":"c4fc1140-230e-56c5-8a3e-b6da43c58660","stem":"$\\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{4}$, where $\\theta$ is acute.","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"Find $\\sin\\theta$ and $\\cos\\theta$.","model":"Opposite $3$, adjacent $4$, hypotenuse $5$. $\\sin\\theta = \\frac{3}{5}$, $\\cos\\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Hypotenuse $5$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Both values correct"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"Find $\\frac{1 - \\tan^2\\theta}{1 + \\tan^2\\theta}$ and $\\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta$ and compare them.","model":"$\\frac{1 - \\frac{9}{16}}{1 + \\frac{9}{16}} = \\frac{7/16}{25/16} = \\frac{7}{25}$\n\n$\\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta = \\frac{16}{25} - \\frac{9}{25} = \\frac{7}{25}$\n\nThe two values are equal.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Substitutes in the first"},{"points":1,"criterion":"First value $\\frac{7}{25}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Second value $\\frac{7}{25}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Comparison"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"Prove for any acute $\\theta$: $\\frac{1 - \\tan^2\\theta}{1 + \\tan^2\\theta} = \\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta$","model":"Multiply the top and bottom of the left side by $\\cos^2\\theta$:\n\n$\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta} = \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta}{1} = $ right side (proved)","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Uses $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Multiplies by $\\cos^2\\theta$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Conclusion"}]}]},{"id":"e44f9543-5d36-5b03-a9d3-5cae6753bea4","stem":"From a point on the ground $30$ m from the foot of a tree, the angle of elevation of the top is $60^\\circ$.","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"Draw the situation and write the relation for the height $h$.","model":"Right triangle with base $30$ m, height $h$, angle $60^\\circ$. $\\tan 60^\\circ = \\frac{h}{30}$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Correct diagram"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\tan 60^\\circ = \\frac{h}{30}$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"Find the height of the tree.","model":"$h = 30\\tan 60^\\circ = 30\\sqrt{3} \\approx 51.96$ m","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\tan 60^\\circ = \\sqrt{3}$"},{"points":2,"criterion":"$h = 30\\sqrt{3}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Approximate value $51.96$ m"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"How much farther from the tree must you walk for the angle to become $30^\\circ$?","model":"If the new distance is $d$, $\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{h}{d}$, so $d = h\\sqrt{3} = 30\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = 90$ m.\n\nYou must walk $90 - 30 = 60$ m more.","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"$\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{h}{d}$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$d = 90$ m"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Takes the difference"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Answer $60$ m"}]}]},{"id":"39095eeb-0b3e-5819-b53e-e1731a773226","stem":"A rectangular field is $40$ m long and $30$ m wide. A path $2$ m wide runs inside it along all four sides.","parts":[{"part":"a","marks":2,"prompt":"Find the area and the diagonal of the field.","model":"Area $40 \\times 30 = 1200$ m²; diagonal $\\sqrt{40^2 + 30^2} = 50$ m","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Area $1200$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Diagonal $50$"}]},{"part":"b","marks":4,"prompt":"Find the area of the path.","model":"Inner part: $(40 - 4) \\times (30 - 4) = 36 \\times 26 = 936$ m²\n\nPath: $1200 - 936 = 264$ m²","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Inner sides $36$ and $26$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Inner area $936$"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Subtracts"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Answer $264$"}]},{"part":"c","marks":4,"prompt":"At $50$ taka per m², what does it cost to pave the path? If each brick covers $0.05$ m², how many bricks are needed?","model":"Cost $264 \\times 50 = 13200$ taka\n\nBricks $\\frac{264}{0.05} = 5280$","rubric":[{"points":1,"criterion":"Cost method"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$13200$ taka"},{"points":1,"criterion":"Brick method"},{"points":1,"criterion":"$5280$ bricks"}]}]}]}]}'::jsonb)
